      en: "The Zhongar Dzong ruins in Mongar District are remnants of a 17th-century fortress built in 1638 by Shabdrung Ngawang Namgyal. Perched on a narrow ridge, it served as a defense against Tibetan invasions. Destroyed by fire in the 19th century, only massive stone walls and partial towers survive. The site offers panoramic views of the Kuri Chu valley. Archaeological digs have uncovered pottery and weapons. It is a designated national heritage site.",
