      en: "Tharpa Choling Monastery, founded in 1850 by the tertön Dudjom Lingpa, is a prominent Nyingma institution in eastern Bhutan. The monastery is built on a 30-meter-high rock outcrop, with a five-story temple rising 25 meters above the valley floor. It houses a unique collection of 24 gilded stupas, each containing relics from tertöns of the 19th century. The main prayer hall can accommodate 500 monks and features a 4-meter-wide sand mandala that is created and destroyed during the annual festival. In 2005, a fire destroyed the kitchen, but the main shrine was spared; restoration cost USD 50,000 and was completed in 2006.",
