      en: "Samtenling Palace, built in 1940 in southern Bhutan at 600 meters elevation, served as a royal retreat. The two-story palace has 15 rooms and a corrugated iron roof. The garden covers 5 hectares. In 1990, it was renovated and converted into a guesthouse, now offering 10 rooms. A 5 kW solar panel system was installed in 2015. The palace hosts about 1,000 guests annually.",
