      en: "Dagana Dzong sits on a hilltop in Dagana District, southern Bhutan. Built in the 17th century under the 3rd Druk Desi, Mingyur Tenpa, it served as a military outpost against Tibetan incursions. Unlike many dzongs, it survived earthquakes and fires intact, retaining its original layout. The compact structure features a central courtyard and a two-story temple. Today, it houses the district administration and a monastery with around 40 monks. The surrounding landscape is forested with terraced rice and maize fields. Open to visitors, the dzong offers panoramic views of the Dagana Valley.",
